CALL BY VALUE
Interview answer:

In CALL BY VALUE, the value of the argument is passed to the Subprogram instead of its address.
It is useful when we want to pass a value without sharing the original variable's storage.

Syntax:
CALL "SUBPGM"
     USING BY VALUE WS-NUM.


Subprogram:
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. SUBPGM.

       DATA DIVISION.
       LINKAGE SECTION.

       01 LK-NUM PIC S9(4) COMP-5.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LK-NUM.

           DISPLAY "NUMBER: " LK-NUM.

           GOBACK.


For BY VALUE, ensure the argument and receiving parameter have compatible representations and usages. The receiving definition above is just an illustrative numeric example.
Difference between all three

Type	What is passed?	Original variable modified?
BY REFERENCE	Address/reference	Yes, modifications can reflect
BY CONTENT	Copy of data	No
BY VALUE	Value itself	No

Interview favourite
Remember this simple line:
- Reference = Original data.
- Content = Copy of data.
- Value = Actual value passed.
